      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[0,2],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=0$ and $b=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(2-0)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}≈0.577.\n$$",
